  "answer_text": "The website **`http://www.rewardclub.me/`** does not have a public reputation, search engine index, or verified business presence. \n\nIf you received this link via an unsolicited text message, email, or social media post, **it is highly likely to be a scam or phishing attempt.** \n\nHere is what you should know about links like this and how to stay safe:\n\n### 1. Phishing and \"Winner\" Scams\nCybercriminals frequently register domains containing words like \"reward,\" \"club,\" or \"loyalty\" (often using TLDs like `.me`, `.cc`, or `.top`) to run **smishing (SMS phishing)** campaigns. \n* **The Hook:** You might receive a message claiming you have a pending reward (e.g., \"You have been selected to receive a $250 CVS/Amazon gift card\") or a package delivery issue.\n* **The Catch:** Clicking the link takes you to a fake portal designed to steal your personal information, login credentials, or credit card details under the guise of paying a small \"shipping\" or \"verification\" fee.\n\n### 2. Hidden Subscription Traps\nSome \"Rewards Clubs\" operate by tricking users into signing up for a monthly or annual recurring fee. This often happens when a pre-checked box is left ticked during an online transaction on a completely different website, secretly enrolling you in a \"membership\" that debits your bank account regularly.\n\n### 3. Safety Recommendations\n* **Do Not Enter Information:** If you open the page, do not enter your name, address, phone number, or any financial details.\n* **Do Not Download Anything:** Do not install any apps, profiles, or files prompted by the website.\n* **Block and Report:** If you received this link in a text message or email, block the sender and delete the message. Do not reply, as replying alerts scammers that your number/email is active.\n* **Check Your Statements:** If you have previously interacted with similar \"Reward Clubs\" or suspect your card was charged, check your bank statements immediately for unauthorized recurring fees. Contact your bank to dispute any fraudulent charges and request a card replacement if necessary.",
